# Slice 12: Euler's substitution. A rational point (k, c) of the conic s^2 = q gives the new letter
# t = (sqrt(q) - c)/(x - k); x and the root are then quotients in t, and the area is a rational one.
integral(1/(x sqrt(x^2 + 1)), x)
integral(1/(x sqrt(1 - x^2)), x)
integral(1/((x + 1) sqrt(x^2 + 3)), x)
integral(1/(x sqrt(x^2 - 2)), x)
integral(1/(x^2 sqrt(x^2 + 1)), x)
integral(1/(x sqrt(x^2 + 1)), x, 1, 2)
integral(1/((x + 2) sqrt(x^2 + x + 1)), x, 0, 1)
integral(x/((x + 1) sqrt(4 - x^2)), x, 0, 1)
integral(1/(x^2 sqrt(x^2 + 1)), x, 1, 2)
# refused, with the reason (before Slice 14 the last one below was refused too; it now works)
integral(1/(x sqrt(3 - x^2)), x)
integral(sqrt(x^2 + 1)/(x^2 + 2), x, 0, 1) to 25 places
